    message: >-
      `html_safe()` add the `__html__` magic method to the provided class. The
      `__html__` method indicates to the Django template engine that the value
      is 'safe' for rendering. This means that normal HTML escaping will not be
      applied to the return value. This exposes your application to cross-site
      scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities. If you need to render raw HTML, consider
      instead using `mark_safe()` which more clearly marks the intent to render
      raw HTML than a class with a magic method.
