      ruby.rails.security.audit.xss.templates.avoid-content-tag.avoid-content-tag
    message: >-
      'content_tag' exhibits unintuitive escaping behavior and may accidentally
      expose your application to cross-site scripting. If using Rails 2, only
      attribute values are escaped. If using Rails 3, content and attribute
      values are escaped. Tag and attribute names are never escaped. Because of
      this, it is recommended to use 'html_safe' if you must render raw HTML
      data.
